  "theorem_name": "ProperPrimePowerContaminationHasExplicitSublinearBudget",
  "declared_proposition": "If A(N) is the number of distinct proper prime powers at most N and L=floor(log_2 N), then A(N)<=sum_(k=2)^L floor(N^(1/k))<=floor(sqrt(N))+max(L-2,0)floor(N^(1/3)). Consequently the proper-prime-power part E_pp(N) of the binary von Mangoldt convolution is at most twice this bound times (log N)^2, which is o(N). Therefore any certified lower bound R_Lambda(N)>=cN for all sufficiently large even N, with fixed c>0, eventually forces positive prime-prime mass and reduces strong Goldbach to a finite range plus that analytic lower bound.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Every proper prime power p^k<=N is counted in the k-th root sum. The k=2 term is at most floor(sqrt N), while every term for k>=3 is at most floor(N^(1/3)), and there are L-2 such exponents. TICKET-188 bounds contamination by 2A(N)(log N)^2. Dividing the displayed estimate by N leaves O(log^2(N)/sqrt(N)+log^3(N)/N^(2/3)), which tends to zero. Subtracting this budget from a positive linear all-target lower bound eventually leaves positive prime-prime mass.",
